# OCI 11.2's OCIStmtFetch2 OCI_FETCH_LAST (#2466): al8i4[10] LAST, [11] -1.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8;
# OCIStmtExecute with OCI_STMT_SCROLLABLE_READONLY and OCIStmtFetch2, called
# through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool
# started, scrolling `select level n from dual connect by level <= 10`. The TTC
# payload, without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset
# column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
